{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"lyrical-integral-waterdogs","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nA runtime Popen trace of the 884-unit wiki hardening oracle on origin/main 72731d3745 observed 1,770 process launches during the production conversion half. One cold conversion launched Pandoc once plus git rev-parse --show-toplevel three times; after warmup the loop averaged one extra git root-discovery subprocess per unit. The changeable seam is _convert calling _pandoc_timeout for every unit, which calls load_config and repeatedly rediscovers the repository root. This is independent of the duplicate legacy Pandoc oracle tracked by absolute-diplomatic-snowyowl.\n\n## Plan\n- Confirm exact warm and cold subprocess attribution and wall time under representative contention.\n- Compare maintained OSS practice for loop-invariant configuration lookup in hot paths and search prior rebar tickets for rejected caching or pass-level configuration injection.\n- Preserve timeout configurability and all timeout, fallback, and process-group reap behavioral coverage while moving repository/config discovery out of the per-unit loop.\n- Use held-out RED to GREEN and defect-seeded mutation before Gerrit submission.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] One render pass does not launch git root-discovery subprocesses once per Pandoc-bound unit.\n- [ ] Runtime timeout configuration remains observable at the documented render-pass boundary.\n- [ ] Timeout, fallback, and process-group reap contract tests retain equivalent behavioral coverage.\n- [ ] Before and after timing quantifies runner-seconds saved without reducing corpus or contractual coverage.\n- [ ] OSS comparison and prior-ticket disposition are recorded.\n- [ ] Gerrit 